0..78 Comment "// A family applied at a call\'s result converts with itself. A type that reads"
79..152 Comment "// a call\'s value runs the call first and binds it, so `tm(extend(g))` is"
153..224 Comment "// `c ← extend(g); tm(c)`; a dependent arrow instantiated at the call"
225..302 Comment "// `extend(g)` binds it ahead of each code that reads the binder, so the type"
303..376 Comment "// it yields is written the same way (#720). The shape is a category with"
377..454 Comment "// families: operations over context extension, laws that apply one operation"
455..527 Comment "// to another\'s result (Dybjer, _Internal Type Theory_, TYPES 1995, LNCS"
528..601 Comment "// 1158). The same law stated as a record\'s field joins once the record\'s"
602..645 Comment "// family field prints at its reads (#728)."
647..724 Comment "/// A family applied to an operation\'s result, met at one argument: `q(g)` is"
725..802 Comment "/// at `tm(extend(g))`, which is `use`\'s second domain at `extend(g)` (#720)."
